      "description": "## Overview\nRead-only public pets and geography workspace; authentication is intentionally disabled.\n\n## Pages\n- `workspace`: persistent shell at `/app`.\n- `/app/home` (`workspace.home`): dashboard.\n- `/app/pets`: searchable, status-filtered, paginated catalogue.\n- `/app/pets/:id`: direct-link pet detail.\n- `/app/countries`: searchable, paginated continent explorer with inline country details.\n\n## Architecture\nCore Navigation, Link, Button, Badge, Input (Text Input), Select (Dropdown) and Pagination where available; Bellini Box/Grid layouts. Reusable `pw-stat-card`, `pw-pet-card`, `pw-country-card` and `pw-feedback`. Singleton `petData` normalizes and caches read-only Petstore requests with independent error states, request deduplication and race guards. `countryData` normalizes geography with a ten-minute cache and shared requests; GraphQL uses builtin `$http` transport because the imported schema lacks an injectable API ID.\n\n## Integrations\n- Swagger Petstore v2: https://petstore.swagger.io/v2\n- Countries GraphQL: https://countries.trevorblades.com/ (imported schema exists).\n\n## Limitations\nPublic demo backends may change; Petstore data is shared and mutable. No authentication, SLA, adoption eligibility verification or commerce. Production launch requires a controlled, secured backend, monitoring and real deployment testing.",
      "title": "PetWorld — Pets & Places",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    },
